---
import SocialList from "@/components/SocialList.astro";
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/Base.astro";

const meta = {
	description:
		"Manas Ganti — research engineer working on reinforcement learning, post-training, and production ML systems.",
	title: "About",
};
---

<PageLayout meta={meta}>
	<h1 class="title mb-12">About</h1>
	<div class="prose prose-sm prose-cactus max-w-none">
		<p>
			Hey there! I'm Manas Ganti, and this is my personal portfolio page. Whether you're a possible
			recruiter (hire me, please!) or just curious about my work, you'll find all my projects here.
			I'm pursuing my master's degree in Computer Engineering at Virginia Tech and will graduate in
			May 2027.
		</p>

		<h2>What I work on</h2>
		<p>
			I'm particularly interested in building reinforcement learning environments for agents and in
			post-training language and vision-language models, across domains like robotics, healthcare,
			and autonomous systems. I'm focused on designing environments and verifiable reward systems
			for training capable models. That's where my instinct for real-world constraints and my
			interest in how models actually learn come together.
		</p>
		<p>
			Most of the work is in measuring things before trusting them. That means leak-checking
			benchmarks until surface features score at chance, computing an optimal ceiling that tells me
			when a policy is cheating, and gating every expensive run behind a cheap check. When a training
			run doesn't move the metric, I write down why. Several of my{" "}
			<a class="cactus-link" href="/projects/">projects</a> are exactly that. I keep tinkering with
			ideas, exploring new ways to improve and validate my work, and hyper-fixating on niche topics
			that excite me.
		</p>

		<h2>Before grad school</h2>
		<p>
			I spent two and a half years taking computer vision models the full distance from training to
			production.
		</p>
		<p>
			At <strong>Inmed Prognostics</strong> (2022–2024), I developed segmentation and detection
			models for neuroimaging, particularly brain MRI and CT scans. That included brain-lobe
			segmentation and a hemorrhage-detection pipeline for CT. I worked with frontend and backend
			engineers to ship them into clinical imaging products used by radiologists diagnosing and
			analyzing patients with neurodegenerative conditions.
		</p>
		<p>
			At <strong>Assert AI</strong> (2024–2025), a surveillance analytics company, I built real-time
			computer vision pipelines with NVIDIA DeepStream on Jetson edge hardware. The work covered
			industrial safety: pose estimation for hazardous-zone detection, PPE-compliance monitoring,
			and automatic number-plate recognition. All of it ran under tight latency and memory
			constraints across multi-camera, multi-site deployments.
		</p>

		<h2>Now</h2>
		<p>
			At Virginia Tech my coursework centres on advanced machine learning, computer vision, and
			reinforcement learning. My work has moved from vision models toward the multimodal and
			generative frontier: fine-tuning vision-language models, building RAG pipelines, and
			evaluating LLMs on real tasks. Most of it now goes into RL environments and post-training,
			which is the direction I'm deliberately building toward.
		</p>

		<h2>Resume</h2>
		<p>
			<a class="cactus-link" href="/Manas-Ganti-Resume.pdf" rel="noreferrer" target="_blank">
				Résumé (PDF)
			</a>
		</p>
	</div>
	<div class="mt-8">
		<SocialList />
	</div>
</PageLayout>
